WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.730
So he's the "key."

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.820
Crap! Let me go!

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.120
Where do you guys think you're going?

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.870
There's no point in going down any further.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.500
What are you planning?

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.250
Not that I'm really interested in what 
goes through the minds of inmates.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.210
Jyugo!

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:34.220
I just like finding out people's secrets.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.220
Though, I don't think you can 
get anywhere without this guy.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.930
You no longer have your "key,"

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.480
so give up and confess.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.070
<i>Why did he get caught at a time like this?</i>

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.320
<i>He's been dragging his feet all this time.</i>

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.580
<i>He really...</i>

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.160
<i>pisses me off!</i>

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.580
Well? What are you planning to do downstairs?

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.590
If you don't tell me, I'll kill him.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:12.900
<i>I hate this.</i>

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.810
<i>It really pisses me off.</i>

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:18.090
You think a guard can get away with that?!

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:22.850
Unfortunately, I'm no longer a guard here.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.060
Enki-san is never wrong.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.480
If he kills, then I kill, too.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.770
Oops, sorry.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:33.890
Ow!

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.740
Let's go!

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.080
Jyugo, you okay?

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:49.960
Ah, yeah.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.310
We shook them off for the time being,

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:55.710
but we'd better find a way down quick.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:56.820
Hey.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:02.860
You're in the way,

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.570
so don't come with us this time.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:30.460
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.030
<b>Sound and Words</b>

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.580
Honey-kun, what are you saying?

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.470
Jyugo is the only one who can unlock doors!

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:44.560
Shut up!

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.450
Yeah, it's convenient that 
he can unlock everything!

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:51.120
But he's useless with everything else!

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.750
He's just slowing us down!

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.850
No matter what skills you may have,

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:58.260
it's all over if you get killed!

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:03.320
That face and attitude 
of yours piss me off!

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:06.540
You act like you're the only victim here!

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.580
I don't know what the hell you're thinking,

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.520
but you're not the only 
one in this situation!

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.020
<i>I...</i>

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.580
What the hell did you come here for?!

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.780
If you can only think about yourself,
then get out of here!

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:20.920
You're in the way!

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:23.030
<i>I...</i>

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.470
Or do you actually know something?

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:28.530
Is that why you could unlock 
the handcuffs and cell door?

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:33.110
Say something!

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.790
That's enough. I get that you're pissed.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.800
What? You noticed too, right?

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.300
That this guy knows something.

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.800
No, I don't know anything.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.120
I don't know what you're thinking,
and it's annoying as hell!

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.560
You and him both!

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:00.880
They'll find us if you keep 
shouting, Honey-kun.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:01.960
Shut up!

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.800
What a piece of work he is...

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.580
You okay, Jyugo?

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.330
Hey, Uno...

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.540
How did my face look all this time?

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:21.200
Way inferior to mine, I suppose!

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:26.000
Well, I guess you haven't
looked like yourself.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:30.220
Honey and Trois are pretty observant,

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.620
so it probably bothered them a bit.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:33.930
Don't worry about it.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.980
Hey, Jyugo.

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:42.870
I think I know most things about you,

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:47.500
but that's because we hang 
out together, play together,

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:49.740
and talk to each other.

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:54.100
You can become vibrant or 
dispirited at the drop of a hat,

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:59.040
so I sometimes think, "We're together 
all the time, but I don't even know you!"

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:02.800
There's never a dull moment with you.

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:07.300
But I don't know your true feelings.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:12.380
You're the only one I can't read by observing
your attitudes and facial expressions,

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:15.040
so "words" are the only clue I have.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:19.310
That's why I believe you'll 
tell me one day...

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:23.200
what happened on the night the 
game room was completed.

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:30.610
You've been carrying a burden that 
we don't know about all by yourself.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:36.380
I thought we were able to take that burden 
from you after the New Year's Tournament,

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:40.290
but something's weighing you down again.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.700
Either someone placed a burden on you again,

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:48.720
or they're trying to take 
something away from you.

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:54.250
There's no need to force yourself to talk.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.480
I'll wait until you're ready.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:02.840
Uno!

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:08.940
Will you believe what I say?

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:25.210
You've never lied to me yet, have you?

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:34.220
He caught up already!

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.720
We'd better run now!

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:39.920
Uno?

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:42.790
Don't worry about it.

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.230
That's just who you are.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.230
<b>"Don't worry about it.</b>

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.230
<b>That's just who you are."</b>

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:53.990
<i>Why do I feel so reassured 
by those simple words?</i>

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:59.240
<i>That's one more thing I don't understand.</i>

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:04.080
Look out!

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:15.180
I'll get rid of that annoying "key" first.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:19.720
Jyugo-kun!

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.600
Once you're gone,

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.770
you people can't interfere any more.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:25.560
Crush him.

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:34.110
One more time, Youriki.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:36.950
Jyugo!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:42.450
Left!

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:50.090
Jyugo!

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:51.840
U... no...

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.970
You're a hindrance, too.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.080
Where did he...

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:05.890
Crafty little inmates like you 
are nothing but trouble.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.730
If you don't want to die, 
be a good little boy.

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:16.240
Now he's been caught, too!

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:18.010
What should we do, Honey-kun?

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:21.760
What?! You're not thinking 
of saving them, are you?!

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:23.250
But they...

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:25.490
The only reason we tagged along with them

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:28.050
was because it was our chance to escape!

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:31.000
But instead, they got us 
into this rotten situation!

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:35.510
There's no need to save them!
Are you stupid?!

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:38.480
Honey-kun...

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:40.510
What?

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:44.520
You are extremely unattractive right now.

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:55.170
Jyugo! Damn you! Let go! Let me go!

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:58.280
Shut up, you little piece of shit!

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:03.990
Jyugo!

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:07.030
You're more worried about <i>him</i> right now?

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:09.220
You're quite irritating.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:11.780
Maybe I should finish you off first.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:20.180
Don't worry. It'll be quick.

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:27.670
Uno...

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:44.230
What?! How?!

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:45.830
This is so annoying.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:50.330
Why do I have to save 
someone who's not a woman?

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:57.950
I'll make an exception, but just this once!

00:10:57.950 --> 00:10:59.220
Got that, you punks?!

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:05.010
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:10.020
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:16.020
What did you just do?

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:19.030
Like I'm gonna tell you.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:28.290
Huh?

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:28.290
Uh?

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.290
Ow!

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:37.330
Ow! What?!

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:39.990
What just happened to my cuticles?!

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:43.550
It's like I was suddenly 
being pulled by something.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:50.550
I knew it'd be too difficult to pull a 
human body. It snapped so easily...

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:54.350
Jeez. Don't make me waste them.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:01.870
Now that I look closer, there's 
something tangled around my wrist.

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:05.570
What is it? String? Wire?

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:11.630
Wait, this stuff is everywhere!

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:13.920
What the hell is it?!

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:16.590
Don't touch it! You'll make it go dull!

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:19.440
The bullets can only be
used once to begin with,

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:21.050
so it can't be helped.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.090
Bullet?

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:23.540
Let me see.

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:24.340
Hey!

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:26.040
I see.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:30.180
You rigged the cartridge with a 
needle and placed a wire inside.

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:34.600
You threw these into the 
wall and then pulled, huh?

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:38.090
So you always used these to escape prison.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.500
Rigging up these wires

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.860
would make it easy to tell 
where the guards were.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:43.610
Very handy.

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:46.600
You're absolutely correct. Impressive.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:47.840
Huh...

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:51.370
Trois! Don't give away my trick so easily.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:59.410
Actually...

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:07.340
If you have something this handy,
you should've used it sooner!

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.420
Are you kidding me?!

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:10.800
I prepped those so
I could escape from prison!

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.350
I can't waste them here!

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:14.980
I nearly died!

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:17.740
You're the one who ran toward them!

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:18.620
Here.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:23.740
You knew, right?

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.120
Yeah...

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:28.290
But once the enemy knows
about Honey-kun's bullets,

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:30.120
they're useless.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:36.140
Honey-kun refuses to use them 
except as a last resort.

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:40.580
I always end up doing the work by using 
my bazooka and flamethrower.

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:44.220
He may be good-looking, but he's so stingy.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:46.130
Damn you, Trois!

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.460
Wait, where did that kappa guy go?!

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:51.890
He appeared out of nowhere...

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:55.800
That kappa guy is right there.

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:57.190
Oh, really?

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:58.400
Wait, what?!

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:02.160
Oh, yeah. You can see the mark.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:05.150
Hey, what the heck does this mean?

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:08.100
It means he's right underneath us.

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:09.030
Underneath?!

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:13.070
You can tell by touching them,

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:16.140
but the floor is made up of small panels.

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:20.920
Like puzzle pieces, you can remove 
them or move them around slightly.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:24.180
Judging by the water 
coming out of the seams,

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:26.920
there's probably a pool underneath.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:30.780
So the kappa guy was swimming in 
the pool underneath the floor

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:34.800
and moved the panels around to 
enter and exit wherever he pleased.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:37.080
I see.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:41.190
That's why Jyugo and I 
were caught so easily.

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:46.030
If you knew that, why didn't 
you tell us, you fool?!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.840
You're too slow-witted,

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:50.030
you stupid braid-head!

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:52.030
Jyugo almost died!

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:54.130
It's his fault for being so slow!

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:57.290
Damn it! I can't argue with you there!

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:02.990
Um, sorry. I'll be more careful next time.

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:08.420
You should say that to Honey-kun later, too.

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:13.800
He said you were in the way, 
but that's just bravado.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.620
Don't let it bother you.

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:23.540
You can do things we can't do, like removing 
handcuffs and unlocking cell doors,

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:25.940
so you should have a little 
more self-confidence.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:32.950
I think your escape technique 
is quite cool and fascinating.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.120
All right, Honey-kun.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:39.720
Which one should we go with today?

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:44.410
Should we go with this? Or this?

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:45.210
Huh?

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:48.400
Why should we go through all that trouble?!

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:53.300
Well, we owe them for letting us 
borrow the game room, right?

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.220
We just saved them a minute ago!

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:59.470
They also removed our handcuffs 
and got us out of the cell.

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:03.230
A gentleman always repays his debts.

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:08.230
Don't say you can't do it or 
something unattractive like that.

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.240
Oh, damn it!

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:18.800
Sixty, eight, nineteen, twenty-four.

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:21.000
Seventy on top, start from there.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:23.300
I see.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.420
We'll finish it on thirty-seven.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.510
Okay.

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:29.000
What are you guys planning to do?

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:31.760
Shut up! Like I'm gonna tell you.

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:33.920
Stupid! Idiot! Fugly!

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:36.260
What did you say?!

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:41.380
We'll repay our debts, 
so stay out of our way.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:47.270
We'll show you our awesome escape technique.

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:49.870
Let's begin.

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:07.670
What?!

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:10.850
H-H-H-H-How did you know my location?!

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:14.340
That was weak. No more than a firecracker.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:17.680
Hmm... Maybe I should've used more gunpowder.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:21.100
How did they know I was beneath the floor?

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:28.580
They must've used this!

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:37.500
Hey, he got away!

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:40.580
I guess he's not as stupid as we thought.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:43.580
I think he is.

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:48.890
<i>I never expected them to use such a thing.</i>

00:17:48.890 --> 00:17:51.460
<i>This is why inmates are trouble.</i>

00:17:51.740 --> 00:17:54.960
<i>I really hate them.</i>

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:01.850
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.070
Those guys got up!

00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:05.600
Just stand back.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.200
Ah, over there.

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:12.480
Coordinates... Looks like twenty-three.

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:20.870
What?! I know I cut this off!

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:24.120
Idiot! That was just a fake.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.500
Idiots always fall for this trick.

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:30.250
What are you people doing?!
You worthless trash!

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:37.260
Perfect accuracy!

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:46.270
Sixty, eight, nineteen, 
twenty-four, twenty...

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:55.020
Not even close!

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:10.790
I'd better retreat into the water...

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:16.120
It's not moving! Why?!

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:28.310
The wrench is lodged in it?!

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:33.260
If they don't fit together right,
even in just one spot,

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:35.460
they will no longer move.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:42.320
Are we the ones you're after?!

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:44.760
Unfortunately...

00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:48.330
...we don't go after men.

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:57.090
Oh, no!

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:07.100
Wh-What the...

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:19.510
Huh?!

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:24.360
Wha... No way!

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:35.360
Hey, you'd better not miss.

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:37.630
Did you forget who you're talking to?

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:50.680
This can't be...

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:01.000
Hey, isn't that a bit too much?

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:03.730
This degree of firepower
makes it look beautiful.

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:07.850
They're way different from us.

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:10.160
Yeah, they're amazing.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:18.420
To maneuver and trap them with 
wires, then blow them up...

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:20.170
That was a hell of an idea.

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:24.460
Get away from there!

00:21:37.630 --> 00:21:41.190
I underestimated you brats.

